# ratings_elo.json is deliberately tracked, not ignored: it was seeded
# 2026-07-26 with a one-time historical backfill (see backfill_history.py
# and PROVIDER_COMPLIANCE.md) so the live site starts from real historical
# Elo instead of a blank slate. The GitHub Actions cache (a separate system
# from git, see deploy.yml's actions/cache step) is the normal place this
# file lives day-to-day; this is a one-time seed exception, not a new
# standing convention -- don't add other generated files here on this
# precedent without the same explicit reasoning.
ratings_h2h.json
# picks_log*.json is deliberately tracked too (2026-07-27), for the same
# reason ratings*.json is: it's the pick-lock ledger the entire scorecard's
# "Locked in public, never rewritten" claim depends on, and living only in
# the GitHub Actions cache meant a single cache-restore hiccup could reset
# it to empty with zero trace -- confirmed live the same day this comment
# was added. Git is now the source of truth; deploy.yml commits it back
# after every fetch, the same way it already does for ratings.
